Z||000000||87ECO5||03-05-2001||02:06 PM||||14 reported shot in a suburban San Diego high school.  Incident happened around 9:00 this morning - California time.<P>When is this s#!t going to stop!?      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>[edited because the death/injured toll has increased]<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 03-05-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||Oreif||03-05-2001||02:28 PM||||When kids can't get access to guns. Of course then they'll go back to knives and bats. With the world today it is near impossible to restrict guns. The only true form of gun control is teaching our children not to use guns. But like all things even that is not a 100%. Dateline last night took 1 week and counted how many kids were killed by guns. The total was 35. Only half were gang related. Many were kids playing with guns that were not safely stored. One child killed was 3 years old by a mother who didn't want to turn the child over to the father (custody case) So she shot the child with a shotgun. The sad part is she had a house full of guns (hers) and a history of using them in agressive/illegal manner. <BR>She actually shot the father, before they seperated, twice (arm and leg) and was fined $45.00 for aggrivated assult! She shot and killed her first husband and they chaulked it up to domestic violence. She was never charged/arrested. In fact she was on a talk show about it too. <P>Being a parent of 2 boys, I worry about it. There are no guns in the house but that doesn't mean they'll ever see one or get one themselves. All I can do is teach them right from wrong and hope they heed my lessons. The same goes for drug usage too.||||reg||9
Z||000002||stimpy||03-05-2001||02:32 PM||||Very disturbing. I know better then to suggest gun control would have prevented this, as no doubt the gun was legally obtained. But how about kid control.  Reportedly this kid was "joking around" over the weekend how he was going to shoot p the school.  An adult <B>knew</B> about this, yet no intervention was made.<P>BTW - now 2 children are confirmed dead. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||loafer87gt||03-05-2001||03:13 PM||||Does the US have a young offender system? I know in Canada a kid could mow down his entire class and get off the hook if he is under 16 years old. In my opinion, by the time you are 11 or 12, you should have a good enough grasp on the way things work to be treated to the same justice as adults. I can't help but to put a lot of the blame on the parents as well, how would you not notice your kid carting along a rifle to school in the morning?? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||03-05-2001||03:30 PM||||I seriously doubt that the offender will get off "scot free" but in California, he will probably only be held in Youth Authority until he is 25.  Of course, if this kid thinks he had it rough in his affluent suburban high school, he is going to have quite a rude awakening when he winds up in CYA.   ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tigger||03-05-2001||04:04 PM||||From what I'm reading the kid was picked on a lot.  That is not an excuse to kill people.  I had classmates that picked on me, almost everyone does.  I can't believe his friends didn't do anything to stop it, all weekend long the kid was telling his friends that he was going to do it.  He was just kidding, come on.  That's gota be a tough for those who knew.<P>What a coward, at least he wasn't coward enough to take his own life.<P>His smile will be long gone after he goes to prison.  Like stimpy said, if he thinks HS is rough, he's got a rude awakening coming.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 03-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroLisa||03-05-2001||04:56 PM||||Nothing can make violence magically stop. A lot of factors go into a childs or anyone else's actions, including their parenting, environment, experiences, etc. <BR>When every single person who has a child commits their life to raising their child the best they possibly can, that's when maybe this will all stop.<BR>Does anyone see this happening? I sure don't.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||blayde8||03-05-2001||05:07 PM||||Aw man that sucks.  I am currently a sophmore in highschool, and I sure don't want to go to school wondering if I'm going to be shot or not.  We have had already 2 times this year where we had to be LOCKED in our classrooms and could not get out the whole day because of threats(bomb, shooting).  And let me tell you it sure does scare me when over the PA the princible tells you to walk as fast as you can straight to your buses, do not stop for anything.  I just hope this does not give any other kids ideas, because this definitly has to stop.||||reg||1
