Z||000011||Raydar||03-05-2001||08:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>I never had to worry about anything like this when I was in high school in the 50's,or when my kids were in high school in the 80's.Now it appears I have my grandchildren to worry about.My heart goes out to the people,students and parents,hurt by today's events.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This is truly sad. To be a kid these days. The worst thing that I ever had to worry about in high school was an @ss-kicking. Never even considered the possibility of being carried out in a bag.<BR>I worry for my wife, too. She teaches Juniors and Seniors. Chemistry and Physics.<BR>And the really absurd side of this is that if a kid is placed in a class and has a history of violent behavior, <I>the teacher is not allowed to be told of the kid's previous behavior.</I> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <BR>I don't know about you, but I sure don't like surprises.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||9
