Z||000014||Tigger||03-06-2001||09:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MoneypitGT:<BR><B>It's ok if the kid is picked on till he flips, just don't let him get a gun right?!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Know what your saying, but no, they'll grab a knife or whatever looks good in the moment.  Everyone in general should be teaching their kids to have respect for other people, young or old.<P>I graduated from HS about 5 yrs ago, and although I miss many of my close friends, I was glad to be out of there.  I remember how down right hateful some of those people were...||||reg||1
Z||000015||pHoOl||03-06-2001||11:47 AM||||These topics always interest me since i graduated HS two years ago, and i'm currently studying to be a HS teacher.  I have a couple points on this.  <P>1. Have you ever noticed that the only school shootings that we hear about are the ones from suburbia?  I don't think that in my 20 years of living in the detroit area, i've heard of a kid getting shot in a detroit school.  Now this means one of two things.  That either the media doesn't want to cover it, counts it as "them wiping themselves out"   OR  kids don't go into inner city schools on homicidal rampages cause they know that someone else there will have a gun and will smoke them before they get too far.<P>Either way, it's an interesting thought.  And i would find it hard to believe that there aren't school shootings gang related or not in Compton, or LA or Detroit or New York.  But it's only the damned rich white kids that when they go nuts it makes news.<P>Rev. Phool<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Hym-The-Man||03-06-2001||01:21 PM||||The problem is the parents, I think that if you are a good parent that you know what is going on in your childs life, you talk to them, the media bombards us with that fact,"talk to your kids about drugs"etc. I don't think that they go far enough, "talk to your kids about everything". Parents don't even know their children, I think that is sad.<P>I am going to pray for the people who lost loved ones, you should too||||reg||1
Z||000017||Jaygee79||03-06-2001||03:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pHoOl:<BR><B>1. Have you ever noticed that the only school shootings that we hear about are the ones from suburbia?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, I noticed that too.  A student was stabbed at my high school, I went to one of those little-rich-kid schools.  The kids there can be very mean.  If you don't fit their profile of 'cool' then you are completely shunned.  So much more goes on at these schools than anyone knows.  There were times that I would be sitting in class and the kids next to me were doing drugs.  But their parents are rich and don't want to get a bad rep so it's all hidden.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Black88GT||03-06-2001||04:13 PM||||I don't think kids get shot in inner city schools for many reasons.  I can only speak about the ones here in Baltimore though.  They all have metal detectors.  They all make the students wear clear/see through book bags.  At any given time they have around 10 or 12 city police officers patrolling the halls or the perimiter of the school.  <P>At the suburban schools though they have 1 cop and no metal detectors or anything like that.  Much easier.||||reg||1
Z||000019||151 in. of love||03-08-2001||01:17 PM||||I don't believe in censorship.<BR>BUT...<BR>come on. These kids get exactly what they want JUSTICE and FAME..<P>Censor all school shootings so that they are not glorified and made into a tv movie.<P>When's the last time a football player or a board scholar received so much publicity?<P>Truly a scary notion with so much at stake.||||reg||1
